content.text:
Review complete. All 8 angles ran in this context; the PR's new tests were run in a throwaway worktree and pass. One process note: per the review recipe I traced callers with grep rather than Graph `neighbors`/`impact` queries (Graph was available, v0.6.0 recorded above); no Brain brief was run since the review scope was fully given by the caller.

No crash-level bugs survived. The diff is careful and heavily tested; the findings are mostly edge cases and cleanup, plus the PR's own open default surfaced as the top item.

```json
[
  {
    "file": "internal/cli/pattern_corpus_enrich.go",
    "line": 445,
    "summary": "A command the user declined is stored as failed and counts in exit_fails, indistinguishable from a real failure",
    "failure_scenario": "The cli writes result.status \"error\" for both a failed and a declined command (codexitem.Item.Failed). A session where the user declines one benign command gets failed=1 and exit_fails incremented, so corpus outcome/corroboration reads a declined suggestion as a failing validation loop. The compact record cannot tell them apart; the root fix is the cli carrying exit_code or a declined marker. The PR documents this default and asks for a call — it needs an explicit decision before merge."
  },
  {
    "file": "internal/cli/pattern_corpus_enrich.go",
    "line": 212,
    "summary": "A FileChange change with an empty path but a set move_path is dropped entirely, losing the add of move_path",
    "failure_scenario": "Input {\"changes\":[{\"path\":\"\",\"kind\":\"update\",\"move_path\":\"/w/r/new.go\"}]} hits `if p == \"\" { continue }` before the move branch, so no ref is emitted at all; the created file new.go gets no edit ref and no symbol links. The empty-path test only covers a change with no move_path."
  },
  {
    "file": "internal/cli/pattern_corpus_enrich.go",
    "line": 325,
    "summary": "The two FileChange parsers disagree: codexFileChangePaths matches the name case-sensitively and accepts any block type, while claudeContentOps lowercases the name and reads only tool_use/tool blocks",
    "failure_scenario": "A FileChange spelled with different case (or the line-level `\"FileChange\"` substring pre-filter at line 268 missing it) yields refs from claudeContentOps but contributes nothing to root inference, so its paths are stored absolute with no symbol links; conversely a non-tool block named \"FileChange\" votes on the root but never produces a ref, skewing root selection. One shared walker over FileChange tool_use blocks would remove both the asymmetry and the ~15 duplicated traversal lines."
  },
  {
    "file": "internal/cli/pattern_corpus.go",
    "line": 380,
    "summary": "Comparing checkpoint_id instead of a files_touched fingerprint re-indexes a session on every new checkpoint even when nothing relevant changed",
    "failure_scenario": "A session whose LatestCheckpoint advances (re-export after a commit) with an unchanged transcript and identical files_touched fails corpusSessionUnchanged and is fully re-indexed (delete + re-insert of all episodes, commands, files) on every corpus refresh. Storing and comparing a hash of files_touched — the only checkpoint input the indexer actually uses — would invalidate exactly when the input changes."
  },
  {
    "file": "internal/cli/pattern_corpus_enrich.go",
    "line": 267,
    "summary": "The ~130-line root-inference heuristic (plus tests and the IndexerVersion bump) patches around the cli not writing repo-relative paths or cwd",
    "failure_scenario": "The heuristic deliberately gives up on ties, '..' segments, unmatched files_touched, and relative paths, so those sessions keep absolute paths and lose symbol links forever, and the scoring/tie rules are permanent maintenance. The cli knows the rollout's cwd (the PR says so); if it wrote repo-relative paths or carried cwd in the compact record, codexSessionRoot, codexFileChangePaths, cleanAbsPath, and friends could all be deleted. Worth filing the cli follow-up so this stays a stopgap, not the mechanism."
  },
  {
    "file": "internal/cli/pattern_corpus.go",
    "line": 414,
    "summary": "indexSessionIntoCorpus converts the transcript []byte to string three times and codexSessionRoot re-splits the whole transcript into lines",
    "failure_scenario": "transcriptEpisodeSegments(string(content)), patternTranscriptEndLine(string(content)), and codexSessionRoot(string(content), ...) each copy a potentially multi-MB transcript, and codexSessionRoot allocates a full line slice even for non-codex sessions (gated only by the substring check), on every session re-index. Hoisting one `text := string(content)` removes two full copies."
  },
  {
    "file": "internal/cli/pattern_corpus_enrich.go",
    "line": 284,
    "summary": "The scoring loop starts at i=1, so a checkout at the filesystem root can never be inferred",
    "failure_scenario": "A container session with the repo at \"/\" (FileChange path /main.go, files_touched [\"main.go\"]) never scores candidate root \"\" because the split at index 0 is skipped, so codexSessionRoot returns \"\" and the paths stay absolute with no symbol links. Rare but real for Docker builds that mount the repo at /."
  }
]
